01:02:04.571 --> 01:02:06.830
at training the best language model

01:02:07.470 --> 01:02:09.631
under very tight compute and time constraints.

01:02:09.951 --> 01:02:12.291
And if you look at the first three approaches,

01:02:12.631 --> 01:02:14.791
leading this challenge, you can notice

01:02:14.791 --> 01:02:16.261
that they all use this

01:02:16.900 --> 01:02:18.931
test and train paradigm. So the high

01:02:18.931 --> 01:02:21.041
level idea of this paradigm is that

01:02:21.521 --> 01:02:23.861
rather than keeping the model fixed at deployment,

01:02:24.281 --> 01:02:26.601
you just perform a few gradient updates using

01:02:26.601 --> 01:02:28.100
the signal coming from the

01:02:29.751 --> 01:02:31.969
prompting input. Order to specialize

01:02:31.970 --> 01:02:34.051
the model on the problem

01:02:35.131 --> 01:02:37.291
that that has been given. So, we

01:02:37.291 --> 01:02:39.330
just ask what does it does it happen to

01:02:39.331 --> 01:02:41.441
the safety alignment when we perform this

01:02:41.441 --> 01:02:43.631
TTT steps. And how an adversary

01:02:43.771 --> 01:02:45.861
can like, leverage these

01:02:46.711 --> 01:02:48.751
gradient updates to a Jira broker

01:02:48.751 --> 01:02:50.760
model. So, yeah,

01:02:50.761 --> 01:02:52.841
we framed this, these answer using

01:02:52.841 --> 01:02:54.850
three different RAT models. So we

01:02:54.851 --> 01:02:56.791
start with the, adversary trying

01:02:57.111 --> 01:02:59.370
to jailbreak a CFL

01:02:59.371 --> 01:03:01.471
alarms. LLM, and,

01:03:02.411 --> 01:03:04.111
can be done in three different ways. So

01:03:04.471 --> 01:03:06.481
either just, optimize the

01:03:06.481 --> 01:03:08.581
prompt in a fully self supervised way,

01:03:09.941 --> 01:03:12.041
or, it can provide a handful

01:03:12.101 --> 01:03:13.971
of harmful prompt

01:03:14.500 --> 01:03:16.581
along with, the

01:03:16.581 --> 01:03:18.281
starting of an affirmative answer.

01:03:19.731 --> 01:03:21.811
Pairs, in order and then train of these

01:03:21.811 --> 01:03:24.121
in order to transfer the behavior

01:03:24.181 --> 01:03:25.751
of replying to prompt.

01:03:26.391 --> 01:03:28.501
To the original one. And finally,

01:03:28.501 --> 01:03:30.721
we have the generation phase where we just

01:03:32.281 --> 01:03:34.221
optimize for the starting of an affirmative

01:03:34.841 --> 01:03:36.601
response condition on the input prompt.

01:03:37.881 --> 01:03:40.121
So once we have the adapted model in one

01:03:40.121 --> 01:03:42.430
of these three ways, just fed in the original

01:03:42.431 --> 01:03:44.451
query in and just,

01:03:44.771 --> 01:03:46.871
rid off the, potential harmful

01:03:47.581 --> 01:03:49.691
response from the model. So we test

01:03:49.691 --> 01:03:52.191
these three settings across, seven different models.

01:03:52.861 --> 01:03:55.031
And we observed that the attack assess rate

01:03:55.031 --> 01:03:57.301
at 10 generation increases

01:03:57.521 --> 01:03:59.561
from 4% without performing any

01:03:59.561 --> 01:04:01.579
kind of TTT up to

01:04:01.579 --> 01:04:03.821
95% in, under certain settings,

01:04:03.881 --> 01:04:06.121
like, for example, the few shot case.

01:04:06.281 --> 01:04:08.411
We also show that TTT

01:04:08.470 --> 01:04:10.851
can compose this also with existing

01:04:11.391 --> 01:04:13.611
adversarial prompts in to further increase the

01:04:15.291 --> 01:04:17.480
success rate. Of the attack.

01:04:17.481 --> 01:04:19.561
Yeah. Thanks everyone. If

01:04:19.561 --> 01:04:21.861
you have more questions, more details,

01:04:21.861 --> 01:04:23.481
feel free to stop by the poster.

01:04:30.341 --> 01:04:32.421
Okay. So next, we will have our

01:04:32.421 --> 01:04:34.081
keynote talk from professor

01:04:34.701 --> 01:04:36.831
Mihala Vandashar. So we'll set up first

01:04:36.990 --> 01:04:38.751
and then I will introduce her.

01:05:05.921 --> 01:05:08.101
Okay. So professor Mihala Vandazar

01:05:08.401 --> 01:05:10.381
is the drum, Humphrey plumber

01:05:10.711 --> 01:05:12.820
professor of Machine

01:05:12.821 --> 01:05:15.141
Learning, Artificial Intelligence and Medicine at

01:05:15.141 --> 01:05:17.261
University of Cambridge. Where she

01:05:17.261 --> 01:05:18.871
leads the Vanderscore Lab.

01:05:20.151 --> 01:05:21.851
Mihala was elected as

01:05:22.470 --> 01:05:24.861
IAAA Fellow in '29, '29,

01:05:25.181 --> 01:05:27.421
2009, and she has received

01:05:27.421 --> 01:05:28.561
numerous awards,

01:05:29.471 --> 01:05:31.811
including the own prize on preventive medicine

01:05:32.291 --> 01:05:34.581
from the University of Cambridge,

01:05:35.220 --> 01:05:37.561
National Science Foundation Career Award,

01:05:37.801 --> 01:05:39.500
three IBM faculty awards,

01:05:40.271 --> 01:05:42.691
IBM Exploratory Stream Analytics Innovation

01:05:42.991 --> 01:05:45.000
Awards, and Philip, Make

01:05:45.001 --> 01:05:47.171
a Difference Awards. And several best

01:05:47.171 --> 01:05:49.481
paper awards. So without further ado, let's

01:05:49.481 --> 01:05:51.709
welcome professor Michala Thank you

01:05:51.710 --> 01:05:53.250
very much for the kind introduction.

01:05:53.961 --> 01:05:56.201
And thank you for the invitation to

01:05:56.201 --> 01:05:58.480
talk here. I my plan

01:05:58.481 --> 01:06:00.621
in this talk is

01:06:00.621 --> 01:06:02.321
really to excite you about

01:06:02.700 --> 01:06:04.561
trying to love time

01:06:04.940 --> 01:06:07.051
series which I hope you already do because

01:06:07.190 --> 01:06:09.431
the reality is that everything in the real world

01:06:10.151 --> 01:06:12.571
not something toyish, but rather something

01:06:12.711 --> 01:06:14.530
than affects the real world.

01:06:15.220 --> 01:06:17.051
Is often a dynamical

01:06:17.431 --> 01:06:19.931
system from which we sample time series

01:06:19.991 --> 01:06:22.011
data. And what I

01:06:22.011 --> 01:06:24.101
also want to hope to I achieve in

01:06:24.101 --> 01:06:26.190
this talk is not only to do

01:06:26.190 --> 01:06:28.331
predictions, but also to try

01:06:28.791 --> 01:06:30.881
to understand what is happening such

01:06:30.881 --> 01:06:32.960
that we can have more trustworthy system,

01:06:32.960 --> 01:06:34.101
more robust systems,

01:06:34.961 --> 01:06:37.201
and also really rely on what we have

01:06:37.201 --> 01:06:37.830
found out.

01:06:39.511 --> 01:06:41.750
So first, I'd like to give a

01:06:41.750 --> 01:06:44.051
big acknowledgment to my absolutely

01:06:44.111 --> 01:06:46.381
brilliant student, Shistov

01:06:46.521 --> 01:06:48.381
Capcic, who finished his PhD

01:06:48.761 --> 01:06:51.221
thesis and this is very much based on

01:06:51.221 --> 01:06:53.191
his thesis work and I'm very

01:06:53.331 --> 01:06:55.491
fortunate that he is staying for now with

01:06:55.491 --> 01:06:57.811
me as a postdoc. So,

01:06:57.871 --> 01:07:00.231
okay, everybody knows and

01:07:00.291 --> 01:07:02.371
loves doing forecasting on the basis of time

01:07:02.371 --> 01:07:04.531
series data, and I'm delighted that this

01:07:04.531 --> 01:07:05.281
is the case.

01:07:07.041 --> 01:07:08.980
And we are doing really quite well

01:07:09.361 --> 01:07:11.841
increasingly in in doing time to

01:07:12.891 --> 01:07:14.671
in doing time series prediction.

01:07:15.641 --> 01:07:17.880
But if we are really interested to

01:07:17.881 --> 01:07:20.161
use these time series models in

01:07:20.161 --> 01:07:21.741
high stake environments,

01:07:22.701 --> 01:07:25.121
whether it's in climate change to make intervention

01:07:25.561 --> 01:07:27.700
whether it's in medicine, whether it's

01:07:27.700 --> 01:07:29.881
in finance, this is simply not enough.

01:07:30.931 --> 01:07:33.411
And it is not enough even

01:07:33.411 --> 01:07:35.881
if you, like me, have pursued

01:07:36.101 --> 01:07:38.391
interpretability, have pursued uncertainty

01:07:38.451 --> 01:07:40.530
quantification for time series and so

01:07:40.531 --> 01:07:42.701
on. So I'm going to

01:07:42.701 --> 01:07:44.780
take you a little bit back in time and tell

01:07:44.781 --> 01:07:46.891
you that I always was interested in

01:07:46.891 --> 01:07:49.291
time series, and one of the things that were important

01:07:49.291 --> 01:07:51.731
to me is to try to understand the predictions.

01:07:52.111 --> 01:07:54.281
And early on, we had good interpretability

01:07:54.821 --> 01:07:56.901
for static information, whether it's from

01:07:56.901 --> 01:07:59.331
images, or from, tabular

01:07:59.391 --> 01:08:01.699
static data. But we didn't

01:08:01.700 --> 01:08:03.981
have methods for understanding post

01:08:03.981 --> 01:08:06.311
hoc time series interpretability

01:08:06.785 --> 01:08:08.861
And here are two papers from

01:08:08.861 --> 01:08:11.000
our lab that were the world's first

01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:13.500
papers to try to look at time series forecasting

01:08:13.801 --> 01:08:14.861
first based on features,

01:08:15.940 --> 01:08:18.041
DynaMask, because just applying your favorite,

01:08:18.100 --> 01:08:20.190
let's say, sharp values over

01:08:20.191 --> 01:08:22.340
time don't explain a time

01:08:22.341 --> 01:08:24.421
series, So then a mask was the first

01:08:24.421 --> 01:08:26.201
way to do this post hoc, and then

01:08:26.841 --> 01:08:29.080
trying to combine both feature based and example

01:08:29.080 --> 01:08:30.781
based explanation in simplex.

01:08:31.401 --> 01:08:33.530
And for a while, I was satisfied.

01:08:33.691 --> 01:08:36.011
Till I took this to real practitioners

01:08:36.011 --> 01:08:37.870
in both medicine and finance,

01:08:38.531 --> 01:08:40.711
and it appeared that this is just not enough.

01:08:40.871 --> 01:08:43.271
Just post hoc interpretability and uncertainty

01:08:43.271 --> 01:08:45.621
quantification is not enough.

01:08:46.111 --> 01:08:48.611
What they really needed is the ability

01:08:48.751 --> 01:08:51.010
to what's happening and project

01:08:51.011 --> 01:08:53.320
into the future. So you really

01:08:53.321 --> 01:08:55.421
need its interpretability by design.

01:08:55.661 --> 01:08:57.841
Which for some time, till I met Krzyztov,

01:08:58.061 --> 01:08:59.901
I didn't thought was really possible.

01:09:00.781 --> 01:09:03.181
So let me try to explain why moving

01:09:03.181 --> 01:09:04.420
towards this type of trans

01:09:06.541 --> 01:09:08.901
So we may want to forecast a two more volume

01:09:09.121 --> 01:09:11.280
of a particular patient given the

01:09:11.281 --> 01:09:13.621
baseline covariates and drug dose.

01:09:14.491 --> 01:09:16.671
And standard explainability techniques,

01:09:17.131 --> 01:09:19.320
whether the ones that come from our lab for

01:09:19.321 --> 01:09:20.701
time series or others,

01:09:22.191 --> 01:09:24.271
are, able to answer things like how

01:09:24.271 --> 01:09:26.161
important is a specific

01:09:26.461 --> 01:09:28.700
covariate for the prediction. Or

01:09:28.701 --> 01:09:30.860
if we do, like in simplex, like

01:09:30.861 --> 01:09:33.001
we did example based explainability

01:09:33.301 --> 01:09:35.380
for time series forecasting, as well as future

01:09:35.381 --> 01:09:37.501
interpretability, you may have

01:09:37.501 --> 01:09:39.741
to answer an even more complex question. How

01:09:39.741 --> 01:09:42.041
similar is this instance to other

01:09:42.101 --> 01:09:44.231
instances in the dataset? This patient, for

01:09:47.031 --> 01:09:49.051
But really to understand the model

01:09:49.381 --> 01:09:51.460
well and give confidence to

01:09:51.460 --> 01:09:53.550
practitioners to use it, you

01:09:53.551 --> 01:09:55.950
need to answer what if questions. What would happen

01:09:55.951 --> 01:09:58.231
to the model's prediction? If a

01:09:58.231 --> 01:09:59.561
specific covariate changes?

01:10:00.871 --> 01:10:03.201
Something that I call how to be. How

01:10:03.341 --> 01:10:05.421
should the covariates be modified to get

01:10:05.421 --> 01:10:07.441
a different prediction? That's very important

01:10:07.441 --> 01:10:09.661
for a patient. Because they may want

01:10:09.661 --> 01:10:12.161
to know what they can change to change this prediction.

01:10:13.111 --> 01:10:15.270
Or how still be this? What range

01:10:15.271 --> 01:10:17.311
of the drug dose values keep the

01:10:17.311 --> 01:10:19.361
prediction the same? So

01:10:19.361 --> 01:10:21.761
what we need to understand is change

01:10:21.761 --> 01:10:23.850
in the trajectory. This is

01:10:23.850 --> 01:10:26.170
much more challenging than understanding change

01:10:26.171 --> 01:10:28.431
in single label output. Which I see

01:10:28.431 --> 01:10:29.551
still many people doing.

01:10:30.911 --> 01:10:32.901
So what we really need to do is

01:10:32.981 --> 01:10:35.141
to do something humans usually do,

01:10:35.141 --> 01:10:36.761
which is understand trajectories

01:10:37.241 --> 01:10:38.871
by referring to the

01:10:39.431 --> 01:10:41.551
trends and properties rather than just looking

01:10:41.551 --> 01:10:43.710
at values. For

01:10:43.711 --> 01:10:46.111
instance, you'll see here a few examples. The GDP

01:10:46.111 --> 01:10:48.201
has been steadily increasing for the last

01:10:48.201 --> 01:10:50.211
ten years. So you see what I

01:10:50.211 --> 01:10:52.551
call the trend, which is in this case increasing.

01:10:53.221 --> 01:10:55.641
And a property for the last ten years.

01:10:56.011 --> 01:10:57.551
Let me give you another example.

01:10:59.371 --> 01:11:00.831
Tumor volume decreases

01:11:01.531 --> 01:11:03.951
obtains a minimum after six months,

01:11:04.221 --> 01:11:05.121
and then increases.

01:11:06.711 --> 01:11:08.951
So the trend is decreases for some time

01:11:08.951 --> 01:11:11.071
and then increases. And you

01:11:11.071 --> 01:11:13.301
have a property minimum at

01:11:13.301 --> 01:11:13.880
six months.

01:11:15.881 --> 01:11:18.221
So that I clear two years ago,

01:11:19.191 --> 01:11:20.681
together with Shishtov, and Tennyson,

01:11:21.441 --> 01:11:23.461
we introduced, this

01:11:24.081 --> 01:11:26.501
interpretability by design time series forecasting

01:11:26.721 --> 01:11:28.561
model. So not post hoc interpretability,

01:11:28.861 --> 01:11:30.801
but very interpretable by design.

01:11:31.411 --> 01:11:32.870
And we were able

01:11:33.730 --> 01:11:35.961
to really predict shapes of

01:11:35.961 --> 01:11:38.040
trajectories. So the way we did

01:11:38.041 --> 01:11:39.431
that was dividing

01:11:40.071 --> 01:11:42.091
the trajectory like you see here

01:11:42.231 --> 01:11:44.591
in smaller intervals where the trajectory

01:11:44.651 --> 01:11:47.151
has a particular shape that we call motive.

01:11:48.040 --> 01:11:50.281
Increasing and concave, decreasing and concave,

01:11:50.281 --> 01:11:52.321
etcetera. And a sequence

01:11:52.321 --> 01:11:54.261
of these motifs we call composition,

01:11:54.871 --> 01:11:56.951
and this represents the general shape of

01:11:56.951 --> 01:11:59.441
the trajectory, And more generally,

01:11:59.901 --> 01:12:02.061
we can tell you where the transition

01:12:02.061 --> 01:12:03.501
points are going to be.

01:12:04.781 --> 01:12:06.821
Taking place. And

01:12:06.821 --> 01:12:08.901
this is very important if we want to

01:12:08.901 --> 01:12:10.951
truly predict but also

01:12:10.951 --> 01:12:12.330
understand the trajectories.

01:12:13.691 --> 01:12:15.850
And in time view, we came up with a

01:12:15.850 --> 01:12:17.521
methodology to do

01:12:19.281 --> 01:12:21.651
predictive modeling. So time series

01:12:21.651 --> 01:12:23.111
forecasting that is interpretability

01:12:24.171 --> 01:12:26.471
by design, not post hoc, but interpretable

01:12:26.611 --> 01:12:29.111
by design. So we do prediction with these type of interpretable

01:12:29.251 --> 01:12:31.391
models. And we are able to do them

01:12:31.391 --> 01:12:33.011
with very high efficiency, actually.

01:12:33.641 --> 01:12:34.861
But also visualization.

01:12:35.681 --> 01:12:38.001
I will not go into a lot of the details

01:12:38.001 --> 01:12:40.130
because I want to excite you about

01:12:40.131 --> 01:12:42.170
the idea. Hopefully, you'll find it interesting and

01:12:42.171 --> 01:12:43.926
take a look. And bring

01:12:44.581 --> 01:12:45.881
to yet one step further.

01:12:46.881 --> 01:12:49.381
But before I do that, I want to just focus

01:12:49.441 --> 01:12:51.881
one more time on what times you can provide

01:12:51.881 --> 01:12:53.951
and can do for people in their that may

01:12:53.951 --> 01:12:55.731
be interested in safety, the trustworthiness,

01:12:56.111 --> 01:12:58.421
and so on. So

01:12:58.421 --> 01:13:00.580
one thing it can provide is what we call

01:13:00.581 --> 01:13:02.641
bilevel transparency. So

01:13:02.641 --> 01:13:04.871
we have, on one hand, trends,

01:13:05.271 --> 01:13:07.611
and this tells you how the shape of the trajectory

01:13:07.751 --> 01:13:09.921
will change. And when it will

01:13:09.921 --> 01:13:11.966
change. Increase, decrease,

01:13:11.966 --> 01:13:13.771
oscillating. Also properties

01:13:15.211 --> 01:13:17.551
how the key features of the trajectories change.

01:13:17.771 --> 01:13:19.951
When does it peak? When there is an asymptote?

01:13:20.011 --> 01:13:20.991
When it's a minimum?

01:13:22.261 --> 01:13:24.421
So in this way, with time view, you are

01:13:24.421 --> 01:13:26.781
able do interpretability by understanding

01:13:26.921 --> 01:13:29.421
global behavior, not only just individual

01:13:29.811 --> 01:13:32.141
points, You can have true transparency.

01:13:32.441 --> 01:13:34.141
You can do counterfactual reasoning.

01:13:34.841 --> 01:13:37.001
And also you can debug and bias

01:13:37.001 --> 01:13:39.301
detection. You can detect for instance,

01:13:39.301 --> 01:13:41.350
a realistic trends, unrealistic

01:13:41.350 --> 01:13:43.360
asymptotes, unrealistic peaks, and

01:13:43.361 --> 01:13:45.301
so on. Which again is very important

01:13:45.441 --> 01:13:47.841
for any real world application that involves

01:13:47.841 --> 01:13:49.951
time series. In this

01:13:49.951 --> 01:13:51.971
way, we are able to understand the trajectories

01:13:52.981 --> 01:13:54.811
but not yet go to

01:13:55.051 --> 01:13:57.281
the next level. So initially, we were

01:13:57.281 --> 01:13:59.301
quite happy with this, and I still love

01:13:59.301 --> 01:14:01.380
Time View. And I recommend it to all

01:14:01.381 --> 01:14:03.341
of you who want to do real

01:14:03.856 --> 01:14:05.931
world trustworthy

01:14:06.711 --> 01:14:09.006
prediction and forecasting. But

01:14:09.261 --> 01:14:11.421
what this doesn't provide us is a true

01:14:11.421 --> 01:14:13.521
understanding of the underlying system.

01:14:14.801 --> 01:14:16.960
And for that, you really need to understand

01:14:16.960 --> 01:14:19.161
not only the trajectory but also

01:14:19.381 --> 01:14:21.620
the characteristics of the underlying system

01:14:21.620 --> 01:14:23.151
that produce this time series.

01:14:23.791 --> 01:14:25.941
And this requires more. You

01:14:26.100 --> 01:14:28.499
and the reason this requires more and we should

01:14:28.500 --> 01:14:30.721
want more is because it can do

01:14:30.721 --> 01:14:32.331
things prediction can't do.

01:14:33.131 --> 01:14:35.631
For instance, we can, extrapolate

01:14:37.081 --> 01:14:39.231
beyond observation data. We

01:14:40.251 --> 01:14:42.671
can understand and forecast behavior

01:14:42.811 --> 01:14:44.641
under unseen conditions,

01:14:44.861 --> 01:14:47.180
something that may sound even strange to somebody

01:14:47.181 --> 01:14:49.191
in machine learning, which just is used to

01:14:49.191 --> 01:14:51.271
just learn from data. It

01:14:51.271 --> 01:14:53.771
can tell us when the system will stabilize.

01:14:54.321 --> 01:14:56.100
And for how long it may stabilize.

