01:27:54.811 --> 01:27:56.341
treatment effect reach its

01:27:57.231 --> 01:27:58.671
and that's how this vary with the dose?

01:27:59.311 --> 01:28:01.551
Is the lower dose ensuring that the effect has

01:28:01.551 --> 01:28:02.581
a sustained effect?

01:28:03.861 --> 01:28:05.961
So we want methods that are interpretable,

01:28:06.341 --> 01:28:08.501
verifiable, editable, editable, and

01:28:08.501 --> 01:28:10.531
generalizable to give to

01:28:10.531 --> 01:28:12.841
our pharmacologists. And clinic

01:28:13.071 --> 01:28:15.221
clinicians. And indeed,

01:28:15.221 --> 01:28:17.471
we can adapt semantic

01:28:17.471 --> 01:28:19.551
ODEs to to allow for

01:28:19.551 --> 01:28:21.581
interventions. And in this way, you

01:28:21.581 --> 01:28:23.281
are able to answer questions

01:28:23.611 --> 01:28:25.691
how given a particular intervention,

01:28:25.771 --> 01:28:28.011
and this is a continuous intervention, so it's

01:28:28.011 --> 01:28:30.441
quite exciting, What is

01:28:30.580 --> 01:28:32.311
the average treatment effect

01:28:33.351 --> 01:28:35.051
what is the maximum value,

01:28:36.271 --> 01:28:38.771
where do you really asymptotically tend

01:28:38.911 --> 01:28:40.731
to a certain amount of time,

01:28:41.611 --> 01:28:43.651
and so on. This is

01:28:43.651 --> 01:28:45.730
still for adverse treatment effects. This is not

