05:21:27.537 --> 05:21:29.857
So in high stakes scenarios like clinical

05:21:29.857 --> 05:21:32.157
diagnosis, errors can have serious consequences.

05:21:32.988 --> 05:21:35.167
While AI agents can generate answers cheaply,

05:21:35.647 --> 05:21:37.327
reliably verifying them is much harder.

05:21:37.807 --> 05:21:39.647
Existing approaches face three main challenges.

05:21:40.206 --> 05:21:42.237
First, sparse supervision.

05:21:42.408 --> 05:21:44.828
The intermediate steps of agents are rarely directly

05:21:44.887 --> 05:21:47.207
labeled so errors can go undetected.

05:21:48.086 --> 05:21:50.367
Second, domain knowledge. Learned verifiers

05:21:50.587 --> 05:21:52.667
require massive labeled datasets to

05:21:52.667 --> 05:21:54.887
embed the knowledge and methods that don't

05:21:54.887 --> 05:21:57.206
rely on labels only use implicit knowledge,

05:21:57.206 --> 05:21:58.507
which is often insufficient.

05:21:59.887 --> 05:22:01.877
Third, biased scoring. Verification

05:22:02.097 --> 05:22:04.347
is often uncalibrated. It can

05:22:04.347 --> 05:22:06.627
reinforce consistent internal errors

05:22:06.687 --> 05:22:08.767
or fail to provide probabilistic confidence

05:22:08.767 --> 05:22:11.067
scores. To address this, Glean

05:22:11.067 --> 05:22:12.687
focuses on three core requirements.

05:22:13.278 --> 05:22:15.297
Verification signals should be processed

05:22:15.517 --> 05:22:17.617
verifiable meaning each step can

05:22:17.617 --> 05:22:19.716
be checked. Expertise grounded,

05:22:19.716 --> 05:22:21.957
leveraging the main guidelines. And

05:22:22.097 --> 05:22:24.177
uncertainty aware triggering additional checks when

05:22:24.177 --> 05:22:26.357
confidence is low. Now

05:22:26.358 --> 05:22:28.057
let's look at how green works.

05:22:28.377 --> 05:22:30.397
We first model verification as sequential

05:22:30.777 --> 05:22:32.797
evidence accumulation along the agent's trajectory.

05:22:32.977 --> 05:22:34.997
That is, each step contributes

05:22:34.997 --> 05:22:37.318
incrementally towards the correctness of the final

05:22:37.318 --> 05:22:39.447
answer. However, computing the exact

05:22:39.447 --> 05:22:41.627
evidence at each step is generally intractable.

05:22:42.078 --> 05:22:44.578
To address this, we leverage the main guidelines.

05:22:45.147 --> 05:22:47.247
We score each step against relevant

05:22:47.467 --> 05:22:49.727
guidelines and use this as use

05:22:49.727 --> 05:22:51.807
this alignment as a surrogate signal for the

05:22:51.807 --> 05:22:53.877
true evidence. These surrogate signals

05:22:53.877 --> 05:22:55.897
are accumulated over the trajectory

05:22:56.117 --> 05:22:58.198
using a beta discounted sum, and

05:22:58.198 --> 05:23:00.217
then calibrated with Bayesian logistic

05:23:00.278 --> 05:23:02.618
regression to produce a well calibrated probability

05:23:03.087 --> 05:23:05.137
for the final answer. Finally,

05:23:05.357 --> 05:23:07.397
when uncertainty is high, Glean

05:23:07.397 --> 05:23:09.578
triggers active verification. This

05:23:09.578 --> 05:23:11.657
includes adding more guidelines or performing

05:23:11.657 --> 05:23:13.837
differential checks against competing alternatives.

05:23:14.438 --> 05:23:16.517
We tested Glean on clinical diagnosis

05:23:16.517 --> 05:23:18.626
tasks from Mimic four, Compared to

05:23:18.626 --> 05:23:20.966
baseline methods, Glean consistently outperform

05:23:21.507 --> 05:23:23.847
outperforms in both discrimination and calibration.

05:23:24.676 --> 05:23:26.937
Expert clinicians also reviewed the stepwise

05:23:26.996 --> 05:23:29.317
signals and found them interpretable and

05:23:29.317 --> 05:23:31.197
practically useful. In summary,

05:23:31.337 --> 05:23:33.037
Glean leverages expert knowledge

05:23:33.947 --> 05:23:36.187
trajectory, aware evidence, and uncertainty guided

05:23:36.187 --> 05:23:37.948
checks to provide it trust

05:23:38.408 --> 05:23:40.727
worthy verification for AI agents in high stakes

05:23:40.727 --> 05:23:42.887
domains. And I'm sure if you reach out to

05:23:42.887 --> 05:23:45.187
Ricky, he would be very happy to answer any questions.

